  "notes": "{貼|は}る specifically means to stick/paste something onto a surface.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n- Pattern: 〜を…に{貼|は}る (to stick ~ onto …)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- シールを{貼|は}る: to put on a sticker\n- ポスターを{貼|は}る: to put up a poster\n- {切手|きって}を{貼|は}る: to affix a stamp\n- {湿布|しっぷ}を{貼|は}る: to apply a compress\n- テープを{貼|は}る: to put on tape\n\nUSAGE:\n{貼|は}る (to stick) and {張|は}る (to stretch, to put up) are different kanji. {貼|は}る focuses on adhesion.",
